                <pb facs="0569" n="457" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg457"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/7456: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-30T16:00:00+08:00">November 30, 1935—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 30—6:51 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>189. According to American military authorities, 10 trains of Japanese troops
                    arrived at Shanhaikwan this morning from the north.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
